# Feature delivery

- Every feature uses `docs/features/<feature>/` and the stages in `docs/engineering/feature-workflow.md`.
- Do not implement a feature before `01-spec.md` and `02-implementation-plan.md` are approved.
- Use stable `REQ-*`, `AC-*`, and `RISK-*` identifiers in every downstream artifact.
- Each stage writes only its designated artifact, records deviations, and ends with a handoff.
- Build UI DS-first using `components/ds/`, then feature composites, then route composition.
- Map implemented behavior to unit, API, component, E2E, security, and responsive tests.
- Run targeted mutation testing for changed business logic and API handlers. Resolve or justify every surviving mutant.
- Update `docs/architecture/overview.md` and feature documentation before final verification.
- A feature is complete only after `feature-verify` reports go and `npm run workflow:validate` succeeds.
